<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Sagra</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the Sagra was fought in the 6th century BCE beside the river Sagras in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calabria">Calabria</a>, where the small army of Locri Epizephyrii defeated a much larger force from Croton. Ancient writers told of divine help for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/locrians">Locrians</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/castor-and-pollux">Dioscuri</a>. Croton recovered from the defeat and destroyed its rival <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sybaris">Sybaris</a> in 510 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-sagra.jpg" alt="Battle of the Sagra" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Jacopo at Italian Wikipedia. · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mammola_-_Panorama_Vallata_del_Torbido.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
